{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pulls/955","id":5376487658,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTty1_c8AAAABQHaw6g","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pull/955","diff_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pull/955.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pull/955.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/issues/955","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pulls/955/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pulls/955/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/issues/955/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/statuses/e305ec2fb3c98734936041af75f502cf6791f7f2","number":955,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Bound repeated invalid-body grants in the original CPU window","user":{"login":"ProfHepta","id":102159240,"node_id":"U_kgDOBhbTiA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102159240?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta","html_url":"https://github.com/ProfHepta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# Exact-head CI follow-up (01a1db5)\n\nThe 01a1db5 workflow produced additional retained negative results: all four recent-batch mixed/reopen cells failed with 130 attempts and finite_target_met=false; both fresh-challenge service cells admitted 7/7 honest packets but failed the original deadline during the second independent History replay. The separate same-packet original four-second case passed again on head 01a1db5 (3.700896235 s) and prospective merge 684d0fe (3.500007489 s). These do not combine into a whole-head pass.\n\nThe mixed detailed report was lost because the workflow did not set the existing TRNM_PUBLIC_V3_CAMPAIGN_DIR. This follow-up adds that environment path under the original always-uploaded artifact directory and updates only the workflow's existing corpus blob binding. Rust, tests, predicates, attempt counts, deadlines and budgets are unchanged. The original nine provider ZIPs (15,541,643 bytes), full failed reports/costs, job logs and source identities are retained in docs/development/evidence/chain-exact-body-delay-20261118/ci-01a1-followup/.\n\nValidation on a complete exact-source checkout passed 3 inline source-pin tests, 4 recent-suite count tests, all 114 source-integrity controls, the complete 2,617-blob corpus checker (still HOLD_NO_GO), and the complete CI contract checker (26 inline pins; native tests not executed by that checker). Preparation failures on the original sparse native checkout and detached local preflight are retained. The unchanged complete-source commit was imported through the native ProfHepta channel and pushed from its own checked-out HEAD with the original preflight.\n\nThree historical before-source budget cases failed their unchanged comparability guard before native execution; CodeQL export timed out waiting for stable analyses; two macos-15 cleanup jobs were cancelled without steps. Required-baseline run 44316662837 remained pending at the retained readback. See the readout for exact classifications. The new retention-only head's naturally triggered CI is separate and is not predeclared passing. This PR remains Draft and production/general distinct-body/Sybil/WAN qualification remains false.\n\n# Observed original business result\n\nThe exact native candidate **974049daa4b72825332b07b59084cb70f4b4c8b5** completed **1/1 independent transaction confirmations under the original four-second attack window on both architectures**:\n\n| Source | x64 pressure | arm64 pressure |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Direct base 119cbdc8, run 44298913299 | 0/1 | 0/1 |\n| Candidate 974049d, run 44309944062 | 1/1 in 3.415648 s | 1/1 in 2.400576 s |\n\nThe actual JSON reports, independently recomputed by the unchanged original validator, have finite_target_met=true and invariant_target_met=true. Both keep 7/7 honest admissions, seven independent History replays, closed accounting, full native state equality, no accepted attacking work and no verifier errors. Actual overlapping false calls are 124 on x64 and 95 on arm64.\n\nAll four base/candidate runs used the original root-owned cgroup with 0.25 CPU, 2 GiB memory, zero swap, 256 PIDs, 16 attack workers and the original four-second deadline. Source identity and original parent/limits were checked before and after execution. No post-pressure drain was credited.\n\n# Why and change\n\nThe base admitted the seven honest blocks but repeated exact invalid bodies consumed CPU needed by the independent verifier. A bounded 500-ms scheduling delay now applies only after a completed native W1 Transcript/Product refusal for that exact authenticated body digest. Delayed requests hold no paid body, lane or CPU permit and cannot head-block ready requests for other bodies. A fixed 256-slot/four-way table has no lookup-based expiry refresh; misses, contention, poison and eviction fall back to the original paid path. The original body authentication, owner/context, verifier, deadlines, cancellation and settlement remain authoritative.\n\nThis is the distinct signed r21 resource namespace. Independent vectors retain r10-r20 history and predecessor-cookie rejection. Budget numbers and the original campaign are unchanged. The source corpus binds 2,617 blobs with no activation or general-fairness qualification.\n\n# Validation and exact scope\n\n- Native debug service suite: 288 passed, 0 failed, two existing ignored; strict Clippy on the library and affected integration targets, formatter and multiprocess policy control passed.\n- Source-integrity negative controls: 114 passed. Policy reader: seven passed.\n- The first hosted source gates failed for stale current-source and literal workflow bindings. Commit 7e3e454f9b18d5d135e72cc5ea373e04fc5a2ef8 fixes those bindings with no native Rust change. Its 58 budget, 25 current-correspondence, 60 composition and three inline-guard tests passed; all 26 inline source guards, 2,617 blob pins and the actual repository checker passed.\n- The native 974049d x64/arm64 cost jobs and cross-architecture consistency job passed. All four native W1 actual-reuse V3 cells also passed.\n- **The entire 974049d workflow did not pass.** The original source-gate failures are retained. Later source-binding/documentation commits have their own pending CI observations and do not inherit a full exact-head pass.\n- The prototype release run's unchanged 512-attempt budget-exhaustion counterexample remains a failure (299,043,264 ns paid). The loop cap and exhaustion assertion were not relaxed.\n\n# Complete retained observations and costs\n\ndocs/development/evidence/chain-exact-body-delay-20261118/ contains a source-bound JSON readback and a 5,388,968-byte XZ archive retaining 217,385,337 bytes of original JSON, native logs, source copies and database snapshots from the four hosted artifacts. Its manifest hashes all 648 provider files; 24 ELF images remain in their original SHA-bound provider ZIPs. Earlier failed local runs, prototype failure, first hosted source-gate failures, native build/test logs and missing cost fields are retained too.\n\nThe candidate pressure phase process CPU was 963,861,505 ns on x64 and 786,206,240 ns on arm64. Separate preparation builds cost 354,869,152,000 CPU ns and 498,487,824,000 CPU ns respectively; these and every native child process are retained. Nested component intervals are not added to whole-phase totals. Energy, monetary cost and whole-research model/tool cost remain unknown.\n\nThis remains a Draft stacked on #954. The demonstrated result is the exact finite original campaign; general distinct-body/Sybil fairness, independent WAN service and production/public-network readiness remain unqualified.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-18T13:03:55Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T15:23:35Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"77ea3ef3bd0928bb9f07455bd0e7d8daeed754dd","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"TrillionniumFoundation:fix/chain-public-cpu-fairness-20261118","ref":"fix/chain-public-cpu-fairness-20261118","repo":{"id":1323087357,"node_id":"R_kgDOTty1_Q","name":"Trillionnium-Chain","full_name":"TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain","owner":{"login":"TrillionniumFoundation","id":262513357,"node_id":"O_kgDOD6WizQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262513357?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscript